    <section id="sect-00001">
      <title>Activity</title>
      <para id="para-00001">The line \( x = 5 \) and the point \( (3, -2) \) are shown on the graph.</para>
      
        <media alt="">
          <image mime-type="image/jpeg" src="../../media/Algebra-1_01_16_12_01.jpg"/>
        </media>
      
      <para id="para-00002">Work with a partner to complete the tasks:</para>
      <!--Q#1-->
      <exercise id="exer-00001">
        <problem id="prob-00001">
          <para id="para-00003">Identify the slope of the original line, \( l \).</para>
        </problem>
        <solution id="sol-00001">
          <para id="para-00004">Compare your answer:</para>
          <para id="para-00005">Undefined</para>
        </solution>
      </exercise>
      <!--Interaction End -->
      <!--Q#2-->
      <list class="os-raise-noindent" list-type="enumerated" id="list-00001">
        <item>Use the graphing tool or technology outside the course. Graph line \(m\) through the point (3, -2) and parallel to line \(l\) using the Desmos tool below.</item>
